  "scope": "T and R are native modal power fractions for each matched axial drive. Physical-thickness contrasts subtract 200 nm from 100 nm and use the 200 nm power as their relative baseline. Layer increments use the preceding layer's power. Successive contrast changes use the preceding signed contrast. Body and compatible port discretizations change together. Original equations and independent flux gates passed on all five drives in each finite map.",
  "limits": "Finite saved calculations at one frequency with the original physical sections and end planes. Normalized coordinates are used only for displacement matching; T and R are fractions of native incident power. This single-drive comparison leaves all-channel and complex-response failures in force. Weak reflection and relative changes near zero remain sensitive to discretization. Spatial and frequency convergence, a reflection floor, and continuous branch identity remain unresolved. The finite paired increments give no continuum error bound for the thickness effect. The regional complex and thin-device all-channel in-plane power criteria retain their recorded failures."
}
